## 📌 Introduction
Healthcare accessibility remains a significant challenge due to:
- Geographical barriers  
- Limited specialist availability  
- Time constraints  

This project proposes a **web-based telemedicine platform** that enables:
- Online medical consultation  
- Intelligent disease search  
- Hospital recommendations  

It aligns with digital healthcare initiatives to improve accessibility using modern web technologies. :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}  

---

## ❗ Problem Statement
Patients face difficulties in:
- Identifying the correct specialist  
- Finding nearby hospitals  
- Booking timely consultations  
- Managing medical records securely  
- Accessing healthcare remotely  

Traditional systems rely heavily on physical visits, reducing efficiency.

---

## 🎯 Aim
To develop a **secure, scalable, and user-friendly telemedicine platform** that integrates:
- Disease search  
- Hospital discovery  
- Online consultation  

---

## 🎯 Objectives
- Develop a complete web application for telemedicine  
- Implement intelligent disease search  
- Integrate location-based hospital finder  
- Enable secure video consultation  
- Manage electronic medical records (EMR)  
- Ensure data privacy using authentication & encryption  

---

## 🌐 System Overview
The system follows a **client-server architecture**.

### 🔍 Intelligent Disease Search
- Displays disease information  
- Suggests relevant specialists  
- Shows nearby hospitals (via Maps API)  
- Lists available doctors  
- Filters by distance, specialization, availability  

